## Context

{{name}} was scaffolded by project-setup with an opinionated baseline. This
record captures the choices so later ADRs can supersede them deliberately
instead of eroding them accidentally.

## Decision

- **Target:** {{mobileChoice}} (`isDesktopOnly: {{isDesktopOnly}}` in
  manifest.json){{mobileConsequence}}
- **UI:** {{uiChoice}}
- **Layers:** `main` (entry + settings + `commands.ts`) → `core` (services:
  Commands, Events, Notices, Modals, Errors, Ribbon, StatusBar, Menus, Timers,
  VaultEvents, Logger, Settings, Vault, Request) ← `ui`
  (views/components, status bar). `main.ts` orchestrates only, behind an
  `onload` error boundary. Enforced by fallow boundary zones
  (`boundaryViolations` gated at 0).
- **Settings:** owned by `SettingsService` with versioned `migrateSettings`, so
  old vaults upgrade rather than break.
- **Tests:** single Vitest lane (jsdom) with an `obsidian` test double;
  rise-only coverage floors.
- **Quality gates:** ESLint (obsidianmd + type-aware, all-error), Prettier,
  LOC ratchet, CSS `!important` ratchet, fallow metric ratchet, build +
  artifact smoke.
- **Release:** `npm version` syncs manifest/versions; tag push builds and
  attaches `main.js`/`manifest.json`/`styles.css`.

## Consequences

New capabilities start in `core/` behind the services; UI subscribes via the
event bus. Changing any baseline above (e.g. going mobile-ready, adopting the
declarative settings API at minAppVersion ≥ 1.13) gets its own ADR.
